stimulus.description:
A class GridStats analyzes a rectangular two-dimensional array of integers. The class is shown with the header of the method you will write.
```java
public class GridStats {
    /** Returns the index of the row of grid with the largest sum of its elements.
     *  If more than one row has the largest sum, returns the smallest such index.
     *  Precondition: grid has at least one row and every row has at least one element. */
    public static int bestRow(int[][] grid) { /* to be written */ }
}
```

parts.model_answer:
One correct implementation (ALTON reference answer):
```java
    public static int bestRow(int[][] grid) {
        int best = 0;
        int bestSum = -1000000;
        for (int r = 0; r < grid.length; r++) {
            int sum = 0;
            for (int c = 0; c < grid[r].length; c++) {
                sum += grid[r][c];
            }
            if (sum > bestSum) {
                bestSum = sum;
                best = r;
            }
        }
        return best;
    }
```

